                        "boxes": [
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "fontname": "Arial",
                                    "fontsize": 14.0,
                                    "id": "obj-75",
                                    "linecount": 9,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 9.0, 470.0, 721.0, 147.0 ],
                                    "presentation": 1,
                                    "presentation_linecount": 18,
                                    "presentation_rect": [ 12.0, 476.0, 295.0, 288.0 ],
                                    "text": "Any external IMU device has its own clock to send (more or less regularily) data over ethernet (using OSC in UDP).\nConsequently a Max internal resampling is usualy prefered :\nResampling types are :\nnone -> clock of the device considering the ethernet layer of the OS.\nmetro -> high priority clock of Max.\nqmetro -> low priority clock of Max.\nexternal -> use of the external clock <gst.clock> abstraction : for th use of multiple IMU receiver modules.\nqlim -> queue-based message limiter for direct incoming message (none).\nqball -> similar to <qlim> but <jit.qball> version which convert messages at scheduler time low priority."
                                }
                            },
